A second OP_TEST_TRACE brings every virtual time to the clock again,
so a thread with Test forgives itself what it ran ahead at will.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call put a unit's virtual time back
Witness: fuzz time-runs-ahead

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -88,9 +88,9 @@ static int op_test(uint32_t op, const uint32_t *arg)
          */
         if (!debug_trace) {
             sched_trace_clock = counter_read();
-            debug_trace = true;
-            sched_vtimes_reset();
         }
+        debug_trace = true;
+        sched_vtimes_reset();
         return KERR_OK;
 #endif
     case OP_TEST_TICK:
